{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/33923-breaking-point-questions","id":33923,"title":"Breaking Point Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-20T09:51:19-08:00","id":33923,"title":"Breaking Point Questions","content":"I have tried to look through the various threads here, and it is possible that I ran right past it, but I could not find if anyone has come up with the questions that need to be asked during character creation to help determine a breaking point for a Promethean. Has anyone does it and if so, what were they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T13:24:21-08:00","id":34040,"title":"","content":"You sort-of ran right past them.<br /> In the House-Ruled thread, I've got a google-doc up (for Humanity) that has two (yes only two) suggested questions to determine Breaking Points, and then some ideas on how you can build your breaking points in-play.<br /> All the homebrew stuff here is kind of hinging on ideas about what Promethean Humanity should be like that are different from the core, since we want the update to not just be mechanical but quote thematic unquote.<br /> <br /> Verge has some good stuff (and a full five-question suite) he hasn't posted yet. It's quite good.<br /> <br /> We're trying to do some different things with Promethean Breaking Points, and one thing we're playing around with is the idea that Humanity starts low (at 3) and then you need to &quot;adopt&quot; Breaking Points in-play to build your Humanity it.<br /> Obviously, we're still working on it. I wouldn't recommend using any of my rules yet, since they're all under-construction and are only up for evaluation.<br /> You could PM Verge and ask him to post them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 12-20-2013, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T15:52:45-08:00","id":34146,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Ben. That is very much appreciated. I will be running a Promethean game when out current Scion game hits the end. My plan is simple: They get to be human and then from there, probably Hunters and then see where they end up from there. So, I need a few breaking point questions to help me determine the best direction to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:09:34-08:00","id":34200,"title":"","content":"Ahhh<br /> Definitely message Verge and ask if you can use his.<br /> <br /> The two I am using are &quot;What would you sacrifice for mortality?&quot; and &quot;What would you give up a chance at mortality for?&quot;<br /> You get the rest of your Breaking Points in-play, though the &quot;how&quot; of doing that is still being worked on.<br /> <br /> Verge's are basically a series of awesome and then you still get to build more in-play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 12-21-2013, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T17:09:53-08:00","id":35205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>What frightens you most about Mortality?</i></b> No Promethean takes comfort in their condition, but mortals seem fragile and ignorant in comparison. Is there something you fear will happen if you become one of them? Why are they so cruel and uncaring toward strangers like you, and what does that mean to become as powerless as a human but no less strange?<br /> <br /> <b><i>What frightens you most about other Prometheans? </i></b>Humans are terrifying and alluring, but despite*their*dangers, they are predictable compared to your fellow monsters. While most seem to share the same goals as you, they follow strange Refinements, descend from ancient Lineages, and summon powerful Transmutations. When they succumb to Torment, or Flux, they can bring Hell down with them, and they can do so much more damage than an angry mob.<b><i><br /> <br /> What is the worst thing a mortal has done to you? </i></b>Humanity is the reward, though humans are no prize themselves. While Disquiet can draw out the worst in them, many don't even need the excuse. Were you beaten, robbed, or even slain? Was the worst you suffered a snub, a cold shoulder, or verbal abuse? What lessons did you take with you from the experience? Do you think you could do the same to someone else?<br /> <br /> <b><i>What is the worst thing you have done trying to impress another?</i> </b>Prometheans wake with few ethical boundaries and a burning need to belong. As Disquiet mounts and &quot;friends&quot; disappear, the Created often resort to desperate measures to win trust and affection. A few unfortunates end up under the sway of manipulators and sociopaths, willing to trade friendship for a few special favors. Maybe you stalked someone, leaving them gifts and terror. Maybe you put a crack in someone's skull to open a door with his rival. How did your intended respond? Did you go too far, or not far enough?<br /> <br /> <b><i>What is the best thing that ever happened to you? </i></b>Without hope, the Pilgrimage would simply be a long slog to final dissolution. What taste of life had you that keeps you going, even in the darkest moment? Maybe you scraped up enough cash to buy yourself something nice, that makes you feel human. Maybe a good Samaritan stepped up and saved your hide, reminding you that you have worth, or maybe you were the hero that day. Little things can carry you further than you realize, while big events can drag you down as the accolades fade into memory.* </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":". 12-23-2013, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}